      "RWW",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data2\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [12, 23, 13]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [10, 21, 11]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 4.67 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variables `data1` and `data2`.\n\n## Analysis of Read/Write Operations\n\n### 1. Operations in `svp_simple_325_001_isr_1` (lines 10-13)\n- **Line 10**: `int tmp = data1+1;` - Read operation on `data1`\n- **Line 11**: `data1=tmp;` - Write operation on `data1`\n- **Line 12**: `int tmp1 = data2+1;` - Read operation on `data2`\n- **Line 13**: `data2=tmp1;` - Write operation on `data2`\n\n### 2. Operations in `svp_simple_325_001_isr_2` (lines 20-23)\n- **Line 20**: `int tmp = data1+5;` - Read operation on `data1`\n- **Line 21**: `data1=tmp;` - Write operation on `data1`\n- **Line 22**: `int tmp1 = data2-6;` - Read operation on `data2`\n- **Line 23**: `data2=tmp1;` - Write operation on `data2`\n\n### 3. Operations in `svp_simple_325_001_main` (lines 30-31)\n- **Line 30**: `data1 = 10;` - Write operation on `data1`\n- **Line 31**: `data2 = 10;` - Write operation on `data2`\n\n## Control Flow Analysis\n\n### Main Function Analysis\n- Lines 30-31: Unconditional writes to `data1` and `data2` (values set to 10)\n- Lines 35-38: The condition `data1!=16 && data2!=5` is checked\n  - Since `data1` and `data2` are initialized to 10, this condition evaluates to true\n  - The `reach_error()` function will be called\n\n### ISR Analysis\n- Both ISRs (svp_simple_325_001_isr_1 and svp_simple_325_001_isr_2) have no control conditions guarding their read/write operations\n- All read/write operations in both ISRs are executed unconditionally when the ISR is triggered\n- There are no `disable_isr()` or `enable_isr()` calls in the code, so all interrupts are enabled by default\n\n## Interrupt Status Analysis\n- No interrupt disabling/enabling functions are present in the code\n- Both ISRs can preempt the main function at any time after interrupts are enabled\n- ISR1 has priority 1, ISR2 has priority 2 (lower priority than ISR1)\n\n## Summary of Analysis\nAll read/write operations mentioned in the initial defect report can be executed:\n- The ISRs can be triggered and their operations will execute\n- The main function's operations will execute\n- There are no unsatisfiable control conditions\n- All interrupts are enabled by default\n\nThe atomicity violations identified in the initial report are valid as the operations can indeed occur concurrently between the ISRs.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data2\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"12\", \"23\", \"13\"]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [\"10\", \"21\", \"11\"]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data2\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [12, 23, 13]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data1\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [10, 21, 11]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
